<section class="section-soft">
<div class="wrap split">
<div class="prose reveal">
<h2 class="h2">Arrivals at DJT / PBI</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>A smaller, easier-to-navigate airport than MIA or FLL, but the same standard applies: your chauffeur tracks the flight, adjusts to early or delayed arrivals, and meets you curbside or at a pre-arranged meet-and-greet point inside the terminal — confirmed at booking.</p>
<p>The airport was renamed in July 2026, and the airline booking code changed from PBI to DJT on August 18, 2026 — same location, same runways, same terminal, just a new official name and code. Search either DJT or PBI when booking your flight; nothing about the transfer itself is affected either way.</p>
<h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:40px">Covering the Palm Beach corridor</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>One operator covers DJT through Palm Beach, Boca Raton, Delray Beach, and back down to Aventura and Miami-Dade, so a trip that starts at DJT and continues south stays with the same chauffeur and the same standard the whole way.</p>
<p style="margin-top:16px">Golf clubs, extra luggage, or a full car for a group — capacity is confirmed at booking based on passenger count and what you're bringing, common for the golf and country-club traffic this airport sees.</p>
</div>
<div class="prose reveal">
<h2 class="h2">Fixed quote, confirmed first</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>Every DJT transfer is quoted at a fixed price before the trip, tolls and standard wait time included. No surge pricing, no reassigned driver mid-trip.</p>
<h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:40px">Also serving</h2>
<div class="rule"></div>
<p>Flying into Miami instead? We also cover <a href="airport-transfers.html" style="color:#B8912E;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500">MIA and FLL transfers →</a>, plus PortMiami and Port Everglades cruise pickups.</p>
<p style="margin-top:16px">Continuing beyond Palm Beach? See <a href="long-distance.html" style="color:#B8912E;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500">Long-Distance routes →</a></p>
<p style="margin-top:16px">Not sure Uber or a private driver makes more sense for DJT / PBI? See our <a href="blog-private-chauffeur-vs-rideshare.html" style="color:#B8912E;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500">airport ride comparison →</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
